I'm proposing a new character class, monks. They (like priests) would have one
very useful special ability. At any time, they could #meditate, and it would say
"You feel at one with your inner self..... you feel self-knowledgable...". In
other words, potion of enlightenment. This would make identifying amulets,
rings, boots and gloves a cinch, and be useful in a lot of other ways too.
This would be balanced by their weakness: they could not equip any weapons,
armor or shields. They would have to fight with bare hands, but because of
special training they would do d6+level of experience damage (or something
like that) so their damage would be comparable to people weilding superweapons
at high levels. The couldn't wear armor or a shield (but could wear cloaks,
boots, gloves, helmets) but they would get a natural ac equal to 11-level
(in other words, starting at 10 and going down one each level). This would
make them damn hard to start off with, particularly if they started without
many items.

Their starting stats should be something like 
Strength:15 Dex:18 Con:15 Int:8 Wis:13 Cha:9

Starting intrinsics:
none

STarting items:
a food ration

Special items:
When offering to their god, they never get any items, however, they can be
granted difficult-to-get intrinsics such as displaced, walk on water, etc.


